WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:02.830
Whoa!

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.120
First Draft
Seisho Music
Academy
100th Performance
STARLIGHT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.750
The script!

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.410
It's the new script for "Starlight"!

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:13.370
Amemiya finished writing it yesterday... on her own.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.790
When I saw everyone in Group A working so hard,

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:20.000
it was like, "There's no way they're
beating us in Group B!" Right?

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.500
It's still the first draft, so we can
make it even better as we go on.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.540
That's why today, I'd to hear what you all think about it.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.450
The 100th Seisho Festival is a really big deal!
Let's all put on the best show we can!

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.880
STARLIGHT

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.870
Yeah!

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.880
Weapon
Idea Rev
June 18
Blade: Surface

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.880
materials are

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.910
As for the blade...

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.000
Can't you make it a little longer?

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.830
You don't want it SHORTER?

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.700
I think having it longer would make it
stand out more in the fight scenes.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.040
That makes sense!

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.790
Are these the rough designs for the goddesses this year?

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:59.580
Yup! Hanayagi-san gave me a whole lot of ideas.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.290
Huh...

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.620
These are last year's costumes, which had hoods.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.250
99th Seisho Festival
Starlight
Goddess Role Costume
3 Jewels
Clean Line on Sleeve

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.200
I felt like they cast a little too much shadow,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.330
so I thought we should get rid of them to make the
forehead jewels here stand out more!

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.300
100th Seisho Festival
Starlight
Goddess Role
Costume

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.300
No hood
so jewels are prominent
Dress is thick material

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.660
C'est bien.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:13.910
That's quite good!

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.080
"You should count yourselves fortunate..."

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:22.830
"You are ignorant of the tragedy that will surely
result from this crime that you've committed!"

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.540
The Goddess of Despair's line here
is different from before!

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:30.330
The other lines seem like they've changed a little, too.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.330
But... this way might be even better!

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:40.660
It's like, the Goddess of Despair's sadness and...
uh, pretzelness?

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.200
Ah! "Pretentiousness"?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.500
Yeah, that! It really comes across!

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.200
It's a repeat performance, but still...
The tempo and the lines have gotten a lot better, huh?

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:56.250
"Life is as tedious as a twice-told tale."

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.160
Huh?

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.000
Those are the words of William Shakespeare.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.290
You didn't know that?

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.120
Hey, my life isn't boring!

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.410
That's not what it means.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.620
We have only one life.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.700
Simply repeating the same story is boring.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:21.000
That's why, to make sure we don't get bored,
we have to take on new challenges.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.200
Even in a repeat performance, we have to strive
for something better, a better stage...

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.160
I think that's what it means.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.410
I get it. That IS what it means, huh?

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.330
It may be a repeat performance...

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.660
No, because it IS a repeat performance,

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.500
we need to have a much, much better stage!

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.250
That's the whole point of the auditions, right?

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.910
Even the lead roles... don't have to feature the same cast.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:56.160
Not to show that we're different,
but that we've worked hard and grown...

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.870
99th Seisho Festival, "Starlight" Act 2 Illustration

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:00.620
That is the purpose of the repeat performance,
to showcase the next phase of the 99th class.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.570
100th Seisho Festival, "Starlight" Act 2 Illustration

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.500
Here we go again, huh?

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.870
The new script for this time around...

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.160
I like it, too.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.000
Yeah.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:26.950
Nana?

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:38.370
Revue Starlight

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:47.120
Ano hoshi o tsukamu no wa daare?
Who, oh who, will be the one to grab hold of the star?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:54.120
Tou no choujou de
At the very top of that tower

00:03:55.450 --> 00:04:08.500
Shizuka ni tomotta honou ga atsuku mune o kogashite iku
These flames lit in silence fill my chest with a white-hot passion

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.750
Unmei no wa
That's just the Wheel of Fortune

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:18.410
Butai no ue de odorasareteiru wake ja nai
It's not like I'm being forced to dance on this stage

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.620
Tobitate
Spring forth

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.500
Tashika ni ano hi mitanda
I'm sure I saw it that day

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.120
Hajiketa hoshi no kirameki
The brilliance of a star that has burst open

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:34.620
Iroaseta yakusoku ni yubi ga fureru made
Until my fingers reach out to touch that faded promise

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.700
Makuake mae ni hajimaru
It will start before the curtain rises

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:42.250
Me no mae de tsuzurareteku
And be spelled out before our eyes

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.830
Umarekawatta watashi wa
Having been reborn

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:49.660
Koko de kimi ni aeta
I was able to meet you here

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.290
Mou ichido
Once again

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.120
I wonder what's wrong with Banana...

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.950
Did something happen?

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.750
That was the first time I've seen her like that.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.660
I do like this "Starlight," though.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.290
You like it too much, Karen.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.500
Well, of course I do!

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.450
It's the first stage play I saw,
and the reason I became a Stage Girl!

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.950
Hikari-chan, you like it too much, right?

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:32.620
Is that... the book the "Starlight" script is based on?

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.410
I found it in London.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.660
Whoa, it's all in English!

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.040
I'll translate it for you.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:54.580
I'm sorry. There's nothing I could do...

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.700
It's not your fault.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:01.030
No. 7 Junior High Culture Festival

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.750
I only asked you to take that on too
to try to keep the club going.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:04.290
Everyone's club activities are important to them.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.300
No. 7 Junior High Culture Festival
Program
When Passion Comes Alive

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:09.700
Daiba-san... Why don't you try taking
the exam for Seisho Music Academy?

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.080
That's the Tower to the Star, right?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.120
They said it'll be rebuilt... for the 100th performance.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:33.540
Yeah. We're gonna be busy again, huh?

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:38.200
It was tough always working so late,
but that was a rich and fulfilling time.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.540
It's only been two months, but it feels like so long ago.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.790
It will start again soon, you know...

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.410
The "Starlight" of the 99th Seisho Festival.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:52.870
Huh?

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:01.100
Drama
Starli
Seisho Music Academy
99th Performance

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.830
You know, I'd always been alone.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:07.330
Then I came to this school, and met friends that,
in a real sense, I could build a stage with.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.200
And I got to stand on stage...

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:14.000
My first stage, and the absolute best friends.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.120
Nana?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.250
I have to protect... my "Starlight."

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:21.790
"Starlight"...

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:26.330
It's the story of goddesses drawn
by the glow of the heavens.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:36.450
This is a story from long ago,
set in the distant future of a faraway star.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:43.000
In the small village of a small country,
there was a traditional summer Star Festival.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:47.040
Below a shooting star that falls once a year...

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.120
Flora and I...

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.200
Claire and I...

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.540
had our fateful encounter.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:58.080
It's as if we've been together forever!

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.290
Let's meet here again next year!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.080
On the night of this Star Festival!

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:08.910
The pair were bound by a far-off promise.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:15.540
However, once they had both turned 16,
on the night of the Star Festival...

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.700
Claire, it's been another year.
But we got to see each other again!

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.040
Who are you?

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.250
Claire?!

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:30.200
I don't understand! Your voice, your warmth...

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.410
The promise I made to you...

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.410
I can recall that it was something important...

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:39.870
But I don't remember what it was!

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.830
On the way home from the previous year's Star Festival,

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.040
Claire met with an accident and lost her memory.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.370
Maybe we can get it back.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.250
Huh?

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.540
Tonight, at the Star Festival that happens once a year...

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.040
at the top of that Tower to the Star...

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.450
if I can take hold of that star,

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.500
your memories may come back as well.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:06.750
Let's go! Together, we will grasp that star!

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:13.660
If you catch a small star,
you've obtained a small bit of happiness.

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:19.080
If you catch a large star, you've obtained a large fortune.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:25.000
If you catch both of them, you've caught an eternal wish.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.540
Grasping the Star means forgiveness for your sins.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.910
Grasping the Star is a miracle of the Night!

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.620
With the aid of song, the two arrive
at the Tower to grasp the Star.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:39.040
However...

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:40.660
Who are you?!

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:51.540
They were sinful goddesses, confined to this tower
500 years earlier, sleeping and near death.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.330
Fury.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:54.910
Evasion.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.450
Arrogance.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.370
Enchantment.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.000
Jealousy.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:01.790
Despair.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.330
I beg of you! Let me claim the Star! For Claire's sake!

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.500
There is no star to give to you!

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.950
Why were they imprisoned there?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.250
What crimes had they committed?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:21.120
Such time had passed that even
the goddesses themselves had forgotten.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.870
Ah... it repeats itself again.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.790
The cycle of despair, that which lies below the starlight.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:33.950
Even as the dark emotions of
the goddesses cut and tore at them,

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.410
the two headed to the top of the Tower.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:39.660
Your star is right in front of us, Claire!

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.040
Please take this... the star that you have wished for!

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.160
My eyes! I can't see!

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.120
Claire? Claire, where are you?

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.700
Claire!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.040
I remembered... I remembered your name.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.040
I'm sorry, Flora.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.000
Our dream will not come to be.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.870
Flora, whose eyes had been scorched
by the shine of the Star, fell from the Tower

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.700
and was separated from Claire for the rest of eternity.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:30.000
And overhead, the stars continued twinkling forever.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:37.000
"Starlight..."

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:42.540
This is a story from long ago,
set in the distant future of a faraway star.

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:46.040
It's great.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.830
Yeah. It is.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:54.660
Despite the danger, Flora had the courage to try
to make a miracle happen for her best friend.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:12:00.910
And, despite losing her memory, Claire had the strength
to recall the promise she'd made to her best friend.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.250
It's great!

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.540
Yeah. It is!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.200
This is a treasure! A precious book!

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.830
It's old! And bulky! And depressing!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.870
It's just an old book sold anywhere.
It has no special value.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.500
Huh?! But...

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.830
What really has value...

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:24.700
is the kind of stage we'll perform on,
and the kinds of stars we'll become. Right?

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:26.700
Yeah!

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:31.200
This new "Starlight..." We have
to make it the best, right?

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:34.830
The greatest stage... my dearest friends...

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.910
I want to protect it all...

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:39.830
on the stage of fate.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.790
And so, I chose the repeat performance for that year.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.910
The stage... of fate?

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.370
The stage of fate?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.790
You mean, with the giraffe?

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:57.790
You and I haven't crossed paths
in these auditions yet, huh?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.160
Still, you said it yourself, right?

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:07.370
"It was tough always working so late,
but that was a rich and fulfilling time."

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.910
It would be great if that time would go on forever...

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:17.910
Drama
Starli

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:13.120
That's why I'm making it repeat.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:17.620
It's my stage for eternity... that single year.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.540
What are you saying, Nana?

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.830
But on that day...

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:27.700
when Hikari-chan transferred to our school,
things got weird.

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:35.150
Drama
Starli

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:33.000
You're my Junna-chan,
and you were never called "Jun-jun" or anything.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.200
I will not let you be called that.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.540
Huh?!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.500
That script...

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.870
is unknown to me.
Anything and everything could change.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.830
This next performance...

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.080
It won't be MY "Starlight"!

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:51.120
Nana...

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.300
Audition
Day 7

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:03.000
Even if it's just to keep this repeat performance going,

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.250
I can't let anyone beat me!

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:11.250
Still, what is all this? What will happen
in the next repeat performance?

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.950
Since Hikari-chan started participating,
it's been an eight-person audition.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:20.910
Karen-chan was always the lowest-ranked,
and got pulled from the cast.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:22.500
But then...

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.750
Karen-chan jumped in.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.750
It wasn't... Hikari-chan.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.500
The one who changed my repeat performance is...

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:37.500
Karen-chan?

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:44.500
I AM                                                  REBORN

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:46.160
No. 99 Trolley Furnace
Fuel to the Fire

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:52.700
Sewing Process

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.700
The fruit has become ripened
and heavy upon the stage...

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:17.080
but it remains tender, and someone must protect it all!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.870
Student of the 99th class, Nana Daiba!

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:23.200
I will protect them! Forever...

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:25.370
Again and again!

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:27.620
Banana...

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:33.950
The seventh day of auditions, the "Revue of Bonds,"
will now commence!

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:48.060
Hoshiboshi
no Kizuna

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:48.050
Revue of Bonds

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.540
It was YOU who changed my repeat performance...

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:54.250
wasn't it, Karen-chan?

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:01.120
"Starlight" is an eternal tale, woven from eight people...

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.330
There is no ninth person!

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:07.200
In which case, Karen-chan... What role do you play?

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:09.330
What are you even doing here?!

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.830
You aren't the same person you've been up till now!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.910
This isn't the same performance we've always had!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.830
What changed when Hikari-chan got here?

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:19.790
WHY did it change?

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.750
What's changed since you and Hikari-chan got together?!

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:29.370
I... Hikari-chan and I WILL do "Starlight" together!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:31.910
I hate it!

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.830
I hate "Starlight"!

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.950
It's about being separated
from someone you're close to...

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:43.500
It's a tragedy!

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:46.950
That's why I will protect you.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:49.700
I HAVE to protect you...

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.000
through my repeat performance!

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:56.250
If I don't beat you, my performance is over!

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.790
I say non non, Banana!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:01.580
Huh?!

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.370
Stage Girls get better day by day.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:07.540
I'm not the same, and neither is the stage.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.450
A performance can only happen once!
Everything burns away in that moment!

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:16.870
It's lovely and irreplaceable, and it has value!

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:20.700
Because it all burns away in a flash,
the Stage Girls are reborn

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.790
each time they stand on stage!

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:25.540
No, Karen-chan!

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:29.760
Seisho Festival

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.910
We have to keep repeating this performance, forever!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:30.950
No!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:33.620
Karen-chan...

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.330
No! You can't!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.540
I'm sorry, Nana.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.080
She and I...

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.450
Hikari-chan and I are going to grasp that star!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:52.330
Karen-chan, why do you shine so brightly?

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.120
Why are you this blinding?!

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:20.500
This concludes the seventh day of auditions.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.160
You forgot this.

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:37.250
Huh?

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:45.580
You've been watching over us this whole time, huh?

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:48.750
Over and over, always on your own...

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.830
I wanted to... keep you all safe.

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.790
Maybe that was wrong of me.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:05.040
"But men are men, the best sometimes forget."

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.120
Huh?

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.750
William Shakespeare wrote that.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:14.000
"Time travels in diverse paces with diverse persons."

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.620
That's Shakespeare as well.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:18.950
Go on.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:20.450
What, more?!

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.410
Uh, let's see...

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:25.660
"He who moves not forward, goes backward."

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:33.580
"The future affects the present
as well as the past does." Nietzsche.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:39.700
"It is never too late to become
what you might have been." George Elliot.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:45.830
"The greatest mistake you can make in life
is continually fearing that you will make one."

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.580
Elbert Hubbard.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.040
Are there others?

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.660
Others?! Um...

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.500
Everyone has their own star of destiny.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:58.080
Stars that shine, the morning star, stars that fall...

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:02.620
Though I may not yet see my own star, I gaze upward,
and on this day...

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:05.660
I, Junna Hoshimi, student of the 99th class...

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:08.250
will take hold of a star of my own!

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.040
Who said that?

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.500
Those are MY words.

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.160
Wh-what?!

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:24.000
This is the first time I've seen you so happy, Junna-chan.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:28.450
That's not fair. I don't know anything about you, Nana!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.500
Maybe I got too greedy.

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.040
Huh?

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:39.540
Every year, to make things more fun and
so that everyone could get closer,

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:45.290
I would play with the lines and add
some directions for each repeat performance.

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:50.540
But then Hikari-chan showed up,
and Karen-chan changed...

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.700
everyone changed, a lot.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:57.870
It looked like my repeat performance would
get turned down, and I got scared.

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:04.830
Even so, those new days were exciting...
everyone was so new and charming.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.500
I didn't know what to do anymore.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.370
Well, I'll be.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.910
You're a proper Stage Girl too, huh?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:15.370
Huh?

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.830
Striving for something better... a better performance.

00:21:19.910 --> 00:21:23.290
Both the stage and the Stage Girls are meant to change.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.620
If you're a Stage Girl, you'll be fine.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.830
So, let's do this together, Nana...

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.870
Let's all make the next "Starlight."

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:43.750
I'm sorry. I... I...

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.250
I never knew.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:56.000
You're so big, but you're timid. And you cry easily...

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:58.660
Just like a kid.

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:05.760
Drama
Starli

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:05.790
What do I do with this?

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:07.330
Take it with you.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:12.160
The time that was so precious to you,
the things you worked so hard to protect...

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:15.660
Take it all with you...

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:17.160
To the next stage!

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:36.450
Sometimes I get worried, because

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:36.450
(Worried, because)

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:44.080
It seems as if you'll leave

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:44.080
(It seems as if)

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:47.620
Those sparkling eyes

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:47.620
(For me)

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:51.700
Only for me

00:22:49.950 --> 00:22:51.700
(Only)

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:54.540
May they shine

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:59.660
Oh, fly me to the star

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:22.910
O bird that has announced the break of dawn

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.700
(Announced)

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:28.200
The hands on the clock

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.200
(The present)

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.000
Make it all stop

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:38.200
A shooting star glides softly through the morning sky

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:40.950
And falls

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:45.910
Oh, fly me to the star

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:57.120
The final day of auditions, is it?

00:23:57.750 --> 00:23:59.000
I understand.

00:23:59.860 --> 00:24:04.450
Next time,

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:02.580
Revue Starlight.

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:04.330
I understaaand.
